WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.650
- Well, I'm kicking it with
Kaley Cuoco and Mackenzie Foy,

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:03.700
give it up!

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:04.533
Woo-hoo!

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.180
From Venus and Serena to
Kevin Costner to Dr. Dre,

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:13.600
some really big names have
come out of Compton here in LA,

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.660
but it's not just athletes and
artists who come from there,

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.850
the community also has a
growing band of cowboys.

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.210
That's right, cowboys.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.627
And you can read all about
them in the new book,

00:00:23.627 --> 00:00:25.869
"The Compton Cowboys: The
New Generation of Cowboys

00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:28.450
in America's Urban Heartland."

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.630
Let's welcome the leader
of the Compton Cowboys,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.043
give it up for Randy Savvy.

00:00:33.296 --> 00:00:34.129
(Clarkson claps loudly)

00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:35.296
How beautiful.

00:00:36.363 --> 00:00:37.196
Aww.

00:00:38.446 --> 00:00:41.070
- Oh, it's got some blaze on it's face.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.528
Aww.

00:00:42.528 --> 00:00:43.361
Hello.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.777
Okay, you look kinda very
cool right now, Randy.

00:00:47.777 --> 00:00:48.624
- Thank you, Kelly.

00:00:48.624 --> 00:00:49.457
- Yeah. (Kelly giggles)

00:00:49.457 --> 00:00:51.560
- Am not just from my Noble Steve.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.880
- Oh my God, how tall,
like how many inches,

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.220
- 32, probably there.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.710
- Okay, that's big enough is what I say.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:59.110
- He is a good boy, he is a stallion.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:01.579
- Oh my God, a stallion.
- His name is Goble Bullock.

00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:02.412
- Well, first of all, tell us what

00:01:02.412 --> 00:01:04.460
Compton and Cowboys is all about.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:05.990
- Yeah, so thanks for having me.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.500
Compton Cowboys is where a collective

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.460
or a small group of friends

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.170
from Richland Farms, Compton California.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.003
- Yeah.

00:01:12.003 --> 00:01:14.200
- We started riding
horses together as kids

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.640
in a program that my aunt founded

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.350
in 1988 called the Compton Junior Posse,

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:19.183
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:21.140
- Which was a nonprofit
community organization

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.440
that used horseback riding that
keeps kids off the streets.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.273
- Yeah.

00:01:24.273 --> 00:01:26.190
- And so myself and my
friends kinda came together

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.023
and was like riding.

00:01:27.023 --> 00:01:29.290
I was born into it, my
friends kinda came around.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:30.920
And these horses really saved our life,

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.730
they really gave us a, a good rooted,

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:37.760
just good energy and kept us distracted

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:40.170
and kept us focused on something
other than the streets,

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.370
so, our motto is streets
raised us, horses saved us.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.210
That's our real life.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:45.460
- Oh, wow.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.110
- And so now as adults,

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:50.444
we're like how do we pay
forward to the next generation,

00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:52.260
because it's important.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.240
The community kids in the community need

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.300
these kinds of resources,

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:56.440
these kind of outlets.
- [Kelly] Yes really.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:57.320
- And so that's what we do now.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.510
Compton Cowboys, we in our community,

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:00.410
giving back to the kids

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:02.560
to give introducing
them to this lifestyle.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:03.393
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:03.393 --> 00:02:04.900
- They bring so much peace to your life,

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:05.829
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:05.829 --> 00:02:07.700
- And they're, recently we just led

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.250
a Black Lives Matter
peace ride in Compton,

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.083
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:13.020
- And a lot of those, a lot of the,

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.570
well, at least the media
tried to spend a lot

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:16.640
of those protests and rides just like,

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:18.470
looting and anger and anarchy

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.646
and just that kind of negative energy.

00:02:20.646 --> 00:02:21.990
But the horses,

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.510
we felt it was important
to have them out there

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.760
because they bring the peace.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.865
So, all the calm that we need and just,

00:02:27.865 --> 00:02:30.047
somewhere that way people
could focus on our message,

00:02:30.047 --> 00:02:30.880
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:31.713
- And what we're tryna do,

00:02:31.713 --> 00:02:33.860
the horses were just on
the front lines for us.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.820
So that way we just,
everybody was so happy,

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.730
the horses were there, they were calm,

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:39.850
and we got a great peace ride in our city.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.690
And it was a great experience.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:42.523
- That's amazing.

00:02:42.523 --> 00:02:43.356
- Very inspirational.

00:02:43.356 --> 00:02:44.189
- Yeah.

00:02:44.189 --> 00:02:45.022
- Yeah.

00:02:45.022 --> 00:02:46.460
- I, and you, I know you ride your such--

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.950
- Oh my God, I'm like, I'm
literally about to ball.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:50.870
'Cause I horses have changed my life too,

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.260
and it's just so sweet to hear you.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.230
I just heard about you guys actually

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.510
through that peace ride that you did,

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:56.530
and I started following you.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:00.300
And I think it's so sweet, I
know how wonderful they are

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.990
and how helpful they are to people

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.690
in getting their life together and kids,

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.250
and there's nothing like it.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.220
So what you guys are doing is amazing.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.020
- Do you get the same thing Mackenzie,

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.390
it's a pretty incredible
thing that they're doing.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.223
Do you think it's just,

00:03:12.223 --> 00:03:14.500
do you get that kind of
freedom when you ride?

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.629
- Absolutely.

00:03:15.629 --> 00:03:17.170
It does so much for you,

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.690
horses and your soul.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.760
Absolutely a 100% they do,

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.160
and then heal in ways
that you don't even know.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.210
Like, I don't know what I would do

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:27.170
at this point without horses.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:29.160
- Well, tell us about this new book,

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.660
on Compton Cowboys.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.473
- Yeah, well, it's
just, it's important to,

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.500
now that we're out here telling our story,

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.730
we haven't been super detailed

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:42.560
and like, get painted the whole
world for everybody to see

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.090
because we really want
people to take it serious

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.750
and go dig deep and look.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:48.790
And so what our book does, it
kinda gives you that insight

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:52.130
into the background, the
stories, the faces, the people.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:54.085
The writer is the author, he was a,

00:03:54.085 --> 00:03:56.080
a New York Times reporter at the time.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.010
This is like three years ago

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:59.560
and he did a big story
on us for the Times.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:00.750
And that got a lot of attention,

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.850
and then us, a book deal
came through through that.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.310
So he just spent like three years with us,

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.790
just talking to us,

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:08.590
talking about how we feel about
stuff, what our views are,

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:10.190
what our goals and dreams,

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:12.810
history, swag, all these
different elements of it

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:13.830
and kinda just put it all

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.820
in one piece that people could go read.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:18.350
So it kinda Chronicles
our different stories,

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:19.183
- [Kelly] Cool.

00:04:19.183 --> 00:04:21.710
- lifestyles, dreams, goals, frustrations,

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:23.760
sadness, emotions, traumas.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:24.680
- How you got there.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:25.513
- All of it.

00:04:25.513 --> 00:04:27.480
And it's something that,

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.480
once you unpack it really blows your mind

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.622
because it's something that
you've never imagined like,

00:04:31.622 --> 00:04:34.780
running from a shootout,

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:38.030
jumping the gate so you could
go hide in your horses stall,

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:41.120
because that's your safe space.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.190
That kinda thing is something

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:43.250
that people would never imagine.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:45.490
Like you will see that in a Western Film,

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:46.400
but you don't think you will see

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.320
that in the city of Compton, like,

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.050
in the area where it's,

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:51.720
you grew up rough.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.700
Now, I want people to know though,

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:54.890
Compton is a beautiful place.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.660
It's not just this like super thuggish

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.450
like whatever the media
has painted it to be,

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.560
over the decades after
the whole NWA thing.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:04.650
Like people spun that
into like making Compton

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.200
like it's just some war zone of like,

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.700
cocaine gang and crimes and drugs.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:09.810
That exists there

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:11.630
which you could find that in any big--

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:12.800
- Yeah, it's 'cause you find it there.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.970
- It was hyper concentrated
due to a lot of factors but,

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:16.810
so we did grow up with a lot of that

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:18.238
fighting and running from,

00:05:18.238 --> 00:05:21.560
and just dealing with those issues there.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:24.680
But it's a beautiful place
and these kind of outlets

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.280
help heal and work towards fixing that.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.520
So, yeah, it kinda, it just gives you,

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.750
it gives you a good perspective,
I would say overall.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.290
- Yeah, oh my gosh,

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:35.640
I love that this horse,
it hasn't like moved.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.960
- It is so happy.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:40.048
- I want this horse, you get
on it and it just like walks.

00:05:40.048 --> 00:05:41.080
- Most of this is 'cause
of how we are raising.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:41.913
(Kelly giggles happily)

